 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-4384: Exp4384 Reproduces New L2 Levels Or Records Honest Lookahead-Gated Named-Gap Partials
 **Description:** Running Exp 4384 either writes `success_e3_ar25_ka59_ft09_<n>_reproduced` when one or more of `ar25`, `ka59`, or `ft09` independently reproduce a new level beyond L1 via `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()`, writes `complete_e3_ar25_ka59_ft09_partial` when all available games complete their bounded targeted active-data plus Mind-Studio lookahead attempts without a new reproduced level, or records `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for any missing per-game fixture while continuing the other games. A successful run MUST set `new_levels_reproduced>=1`, `reproducible_total_levels>=34`, preserve exactly one `per_game_scorecard` row for each target in order, set `verifier_is_oracle=true`, preserve all three `world_model_paths`, record active-data summaries and `lookahead_fidelity` for every available game, set `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from active dataset hashes, world-model hashes, skill files, per-game plans, reproduction-gate results, verifier rounds, lookahead-fidelity checks, residual gap classes, and random seed. A partial run MUST set unsolved games to `offline_reproduced=false`, keep `new_reproduced_level` equal to the prior best level, persist each game's best verifier accuracy, K-step lookahead fidelity, and targeted active-data coverage, and record the residual gap classes `ar25_l2_action7_undo_stack_hidden_rule_gap`, `ka59_l2_hidden_step_counter_hud_register_gap`, and/or `ft09_l2_residual_world_model_mismatch_gap` rather than claiming a solve.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-4395: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Named Hidden-Rule Gap Retry With Object-Relevance And Per-Register Fidelity Gate Exp4395
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4395 as an offline, no-leaderboard checkpoint over exactly `ar25`, `ka59`, and `ft09`, reusing Exp 4384 active data and the existing world-model deliverables while adding a per-register lookahead-fidelity gate and the outer-loop ka59 object-relevance discriminator. It MUST check that each offline `environment_files/<game>/` directory is non-empty, that the executable-world-model harness and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce` import, that TRM training is stood down, and that no leaderboard submission is attempted; missing environments MUST record `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for that game while continuing the others. For each game the workflow SHALL preserve a checkpoint row before moving to the next game, carry forward prior best L1, record verifier accuracy and lookahead fidelity per round, block planning until the named hidden register reaches the fidelity threshold, and count a new level only when an offline reproduction gate proves a level beyond the prior best. The ka59 row SHALL include an `object_relevance_discriminator` record describing the click-capable / multi-object-push provenance commits, the active object candidates, the selected relevance hypothesis, and whether object relevance raised the hidden step-counter HUD lookahead fidelity enough to permit planning. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4395_e3_blocked_mechanic_tails_ar25_ka59_ft09.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `per_game_scorecard`, bare int `new_levels_reproduced`, bare int `reproducible_total_levels`, `world_model_paths`, bare bool `verifier_is_oracle=true`, `preconditions_checked`, bare int `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, and `field_principles` matching the task's required artifact fields.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-4395: Exp4395 Either Reproduces Named L2 Progress Or Records Honest Object-Relevance-Gated Partials
+**Description:** Running Exp 4395 either writes `success_e3_ar25_ka59_ft09_<n>_reproduced` when one or more target games reproduce a new level beyond L1 through `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()`, writes `complete_e3_ar25_ka59_ft09_partial` when all available games complete the bounded per-register fidelity-gated retry without a new reproduced level, or records `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for any missing per-game fixture while continuing the others. A successful run MUST set `new_levels_reproduced>=1`, `reproducible_total_levels>=34`, preserve one scorecard row for each target in order, set `offline_reproduced=true` only for rows whose reproduction result reaches the target level, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the object-relevance discriminator, extended world models, plans, reproduction results, scorecards, and random seed. A partial run MUST keep `new_reproduced_level` equal to the prior best, set `offline_reproduced=false`, preserve best fidelity and verifier accuracy, record the residual gap classes `ar25_l2_action7_undo_stack_hidden_rule_gap`, `ka59_l2_object_relevance_step_counter_hud_register_gap`, and/or `ft09_l2_residual_world_model_mismatch_gap`, and include the ka59 object-relevance discriminator outcome rather than claiming click mechanics or brute search are still the blocker.
